-- title:
--   Unramified descent of completed local rings at an ordinary point
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain, $q$ a prime with $q \ge 5$, $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \neq q$; assume $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ while $\ell$ and $M'$ are units in $A$, and that the residue field of $A$ is finite. Assume the two stability hypotheses: for every $A$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve over $T$ and every variable change $C$, a level-$\ell$ datum $D$ (four coordinates satisfying the affine equation, with $\operatorname{pre}\Psi_\ell$ vanishing at both $x$-coordinates and both independence elements units) stays such a datum after the variable change, and a polynomial $h$ with $\mathrm{IsGamma0PowAt}\ W\ p\ k$ (the two-torsion-kernel condition when $p^k=2$, otherwise the cyclic generator-kernel conditions on degree, leading coefficient, divisibility of $\operatorname{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$ and of the shifted numerators) stays such after applying `kernelVariableChangeDeg`. Fix group laws $\mathcal G$ over $A$ (a relative group law on the projective model of each curve with unit discriminant over each $A$-algebra) which are chord-tangent and have the origin as identity, a level transport $\mathcal T$ for Drinfeld $q$-bases which is a section transport, and the hypotheses that every variable change and every coefficient map is realised by a graded ring homomorphism of projective-model rings with the stated condition on irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be a package representing the level moduli datum attached to `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q`, i.e. to the product of the $\Gamma_0$-prime-power component at $M'$, the level-$\ell$ component and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component, with $B_0 = P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A$; let $\mathfrak p$ be a minimal prime of $B_0$. Assume further that $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi)$ with $\varpi^{q-1} = \varepsilon q$ for a unit $\varepsilon$, that $\zeta \in A$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, that $xr$ is a raw datum over $B_0$ (a curve with unit discriminant together with level data) whose class in the point set is the universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$, and that $x$ is a maximal ideal of $B_0/\mathfrak p$ containing the image of $\mathfrak m_A$. Finally let $F_0$ be a formal group over $(B_0/\mathfrak p)/x$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law of the curve of $xr$ reduced modulo $\mathfrak p$ and then modulo $x$, and assume $F_0$ is ordinary in the sense that its $q$-th iterate series (defined by $[0] = 0$ and $[n+1](Z) = F_0([n](Z), Z)$) equals $u \cdot X^q$ for some unit power series $u$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with $\mathfrak m_{A_0} = (q)$ and finite residue field, together with stability hypotheses, group laws $\mathcal G_0$ (chord-tangent, origin the identity), a section transport $\mathcal T_0$ and the two realisation hypotheses over $A_0$, a package $P^u$ for `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q` with $P^u.B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, a raw datum $xu$ over $P^u.B_0$ whose class is the universal point, a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m^u$ of $P^u.B_0$ containing the image of $q$, and a formal group $F_0^u$ over $P^u.B_0/\mathfrak m^u$ equal to the fixed formal group law of the curve of $xu$ modulo $\mathfrak m^u$ and likewise ordinary, such that the $x$-adic completion of $B_0/\mathfrak p$ and the $\mathfrak m^u$-adic completion of $P^u.B_0$ are isomorphic as rings.
--
--   This is the descent step that replaces a base containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity by an absolutely unramified discrete valuation ring: the completed local ring of a component of the full-level fine moduli ring at an ordinary closed point is identified with a completed local ring of the corresponding package over a base with maximal ideal generated by $q$, where the deformation-theoretic presentations are available. It is used in the proof that the residue field tensored with such a completion is reduced.
